# Build context for the FRONTEND image (docker-compose `frontend` builds from `.`).
# The backend service builds from ./backend with its own .dockerignore, so nothing
# here affects it.
#
# Without this file the context was 3.0GB and every byte was sent to the daemon and
# then baked in by `COPY . .`: 1.5GB of backend/data (mostly picks.db backups), 636MB
# of node_modules, 567MB of backend/venv, 127MB of stale .next output. On a 5.8GB box
# where the runbook already warns this build can OOM, that was the cheapest risk to
# remove. Context drops to roughly 50MB.

# Installed fresh by `npm ci` inside the image. Leaving it here was worse than
# wasteful: `COPY . .` runs AFTER `npm ci` and would overwrite the image's freshly
# installed tree with the host's.
node_modules

# Build output -- regenerated by `npm run build`. Copying a stale one in only risks
# confusing the build with artifacts from another commit.
.next
out

# Not needed to build the frontend, and nothing under pages/components/lib/services
# imports from it. This is the 1.5GB of databases and 567MB virtualenv.
backend

.git
.gitignore

# Databases and their backups, wherever they land.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.bak
*.bak-*

# Local tooling / agent state, logs, caches, scratch.
.claude
.hermes
.context
*.log
__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.venv*
venv

# Docs and specs -- read by humans and agents, never by the build.
docs
*.md
!README.md

.env
.env.*
.DS_Store
